(word "gen.3.5#12" (english "him/it") (why "ἀπ’ αὐτοῦ is the tree, not θεός (word 4); the open form."))
(word "gen.3.7#8" (subject "they") (why "ἔγνωσαν: the two people knew, not their eyes; the καί-joined verb would continue \"the eyes\"."))
(word "gen.4.1#9" (subject "he/she/it") (why "συνέλαβεν: the subject changes to Eve, named as the object of ἔγνω; joined by καί it read \"Adam ... conceived\" (as 2:21)."))
(word "gen.4.13#11" (english "than") (why "Μείζων ... τοῦ ἀφεθῆναί με: the genitive of comparison, \"greater ... than my being forgiven\"; \"of\" loses the comparison."))
(word "gen.8.12#13" (subject "he/she/it") (why "οὐ προσέθετο: the dove (the object τὴν περιστεράν) did not return, not Noah."))
(word "gen.18.7#8" (subject "he/she/it") (why "ἔλαβον as printed is first singular or third plural, but the only actor is Abraham (he runs and gives to the servant); the open singular pronoun. Check the scan: ἔλαβεν may be meant."))
(word "gen.18.13#6" (sense why) (why "Ὅτι for τί ὅτι, interrogative: \"Why did Sarah laugh ...?\", not a statement."))
(word "gen.19.26#10" (subject "he/she/it") (why "ἐγένετο στήλη ἁλός: the woman became a pillar of salt; στήλη is the predicate, so the open pronoun and Greek order."))
(word "gen.24.24#13" (tag "N-DSM") (why "ὃν ἔτεκεν αὐτῷ Ναχώρ: Ναχώρ is dative in apposition to αὐτῷ; Milcah bore, not Nahor."))
(word "gen.24.46#22" (tag "V-2AAI-1S") (why "ἔπιον: \"I drank\", the servant telling his own story."))
(word "gen.28.17#13" (english "[anything] rather than") (why "οὐκ ἔστιν τοῦτο ἀλλ’ ἢ οἶκος θεοῦ: \"this is not [anything] rather than house of God\" (nothing but); the phrase's bare \"rather\" would deny it."))
